{"id":28700,"slug":"akira-kurosawa-s-dreams","title":"Akira Kurosawa’s Dreams","year":1990,"country":"Japan, United States","duration":120,"spine":842,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28700-akira-kurosawa-s-dreams","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/e9fc8a91b2f9ebe10efb6edde367dffe/LRIg86I1YijdtiaQ7G1aWN6USnhprt_large.jpg","description":"Unfolding in a series of eight mythic vignettes, this late work by Akira Kurosawa was inspired by the beloved director’s own nighttime visions, along with stories from Japanese folklore. In a visually sumptuous journey through the master’s imagination, tales of childlike wonder give way to apocalyptic apparitions: a young boy stumbles on a fox wedding in a forest; a soldier confronts the ghosts of the war dead; a power-plant meltdown smothers a seaside landscape in radioactive fumes. Interspersed with reflections on the redemptive power of creation, including a richly textured tribute to Vincent van Gogh (who is played by Martin Scorsese), Akira Kurosawa’s Dreams is both a showcase for its maker’s artistry at its most unbridled and a deeply personal lament for a world at the mercy of human ignorance.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Akira Kurosawa","slug":"akira-kurosawa"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Akira Terao","role":"I","slug":"akira-terao"},{"actor":"Mitsuko Baisho","role":"Mother","slug":"mitsuko-baisho"},{"actor":"Mieko Harada","role":"Snow woman","slug":"mieko-harada"},{"actor":"Toshie Negishi","role":"Woman carrying a child (“Mount Fuji in Red”)","slug":"toshie-negishi"},{"actor":"Mitsunori Isaki","role":"I as an adolescent (“The Peach Orchard”)","slug":"mitsunori-isaki"},{"actor":"Toshihiko Nakano","role":"I as a young boy (“Sunshine Through the Rain”)","slug":"toshihiko-nakano"},{"actor":"Yoshitaka Zushi","role":"Private Noguchi (“The Tunnel”)","slug":"yoshitaka-zushi"},{"actor":"Hisashi Igawa","role":"Power-plant worker (“Mount Fuji in Red”)","slug":"hisashi-igawa"},{"actor":"Chosuke I